From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:29:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 318/342] tcp: reset on data that arrives after the socket was
 closed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A connection closed normally (FIN) while the peer kept sending queued what
arrived for a reader that no longer existed, and held it until the 2 MSL
timer freed the endpoint: on the test board, 4 senders took used memory
from 250 to 1,503 MB in 4 minutes (1,062 connections), the rest of the
memory left in empty slabs of the net buffer caches. _Disconnect() already
resets when unread data is queued at close; RFC 2525 § 2.17 asks the same
"if any new data is received". After Free() (the application has closed
the socket, FLAG_CLOSED), new data in FINISH_SENT or FINISH_ACKNOWLEDGED
now gets a reset, and the endpoint closes through _Close(), whose
FLAG_DELETE_ON_CLOSE lets SegmentReceived() release the reference Free()
took, once, as before. A half-close (shutdown(SHUT_WR)) keeps receiving.
Same load afterwards: used memory flat at 250 MB over 66,715 connections.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../kernel/network/protocols/tcp/TCPEndpoint.cpp   | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/tcp/TCPEndpoint.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/tcp/TCPEndpoint.cpp
index 7a6ed8b3de..795ff8babc 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/tcp/TCPEndpoint.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/tcp/TCPEndpoint.cpp
@@ -1925,6 +1925,20 @@ TCPEndpoint::_Receive(tcp_segment_header& segment, net_buffer* buffer)
 	// the size as we still need it later.
 	const uint32 bufferSize = buffer->size;
 
+	// New data after the application closed the socket has no reader: the
+	// peer doesn't know, so reset instead of keeping what arrives until the
+	// time wait ends ("or if any new data is received", RFC 2525 § 2.17;
+	// _Disconnect() covers data already queued at close). A half-close
+	// (shutdown(SHUT_WR)) doesn't set FLAG_CLOSED and keeps receiving.
+	if (bufferSize > 0 && (fFlags & FLAG_CLOSED) != 0
+		&& (fState == FINISH_SENT || fState == FINISH_ACKNOWLEDGED)
+		&& tcp_sequence(segment.sequence + bufferSize) > fReceiveNext) {
+		TRACE("Receive(): data after close, resetting");
+		_SendReset(true);
+		_Close();
+		return DROP;
+	}
+
 	if ((bufferSize > 0 || (segment.flags & TCP_FLAG_FINISH) != 0)
 		&& _ShouldReceive())
 		notify = _AddData(segment, buffer);
